h adapters and  then we have a 12 volt one like you  typically have in your car for travel  accessories so that is great and the  ports above we have the charging port we  have a little breaker switch and then we  have the solar connector which I'll talk  about with the Delta II you can run over  90 percent of your appliances and when  we went camping the first thing that we  did is we made waffles with this thing  and those take a lot of power and  typically I would have to do it inside  my trailer if I had hookups but we  didn't have hookups here so I wouldn't  be able to anyways and our table was  really far away from the campground  we're at and I was able to grab this  thing and go out and do that with my  kids it was awesome now during that trip  we did a lot of things we used a coffee  maker we use this bug zapper which was  really convenient just be able to have  anything any of those kind of things  anywhere we're at and with that we  actually boiled water with a kettle and  those things take so much power you  would not be able to do that but with  this thing we could and this thing's not  just for camping I found a bunch of uses  for it at my house for example my kid  left my tractor lights on so the battery  died and I have that about 150 feet away  from my garage so I'd have to run  multiple extensions or have to push it  back to my house instead I grabbed this  thing I brought it over I plugged in a  little battery charger and charged it  right up it was super convenient and  this thing is surprisingly light for the  capacity it's 27 pounds when I took it  out of the box I was really surprised by  how lightweight it was and because of  that I started taking it more places for  example we went to the beach and I had  my inflator with me and I think I need  to charge up the battery so I literally  just grabbed it with me brought it down  plugged it in had no problems at all so  it's super convenient for whatever  you're doing now this thing lasts a  surp